# Tale of Einbroch (Barde)  |  Skill 8114  |  Sprache: Mittelhochdeutsch
# Quelle: Suno aligned_lyrics (Tale of Einbroch - Male.mp3), Zeitbasis = Wiedergabestart der WAV
# ms<TAB>original<TAB>english   (english leer = Vocable/Chor -> keine Blase; ~ = Start geschaetzt, Suno-Alignment unsicher)
# [Intro – pickaxe on stone, then anvil answers, pit crew hums]
21774	(Mmmmm… mmm-brrum… mmmmm…)	
21847	(Mmmmm… mmm-brrum… mmmmm…)	
# [Bar 1, Stollen 1 – pit crew, hoarse, hum underneath]
21952	Ez was ein tac als ander tage,	It was a day like any other day,
25931	wir vuoren in bi grawem lieht.	we went down in the grey light.
29548	Diu lampe bran, der hamer sluoc –	The lamp burned, the hammer struck –
33175	und niemen sach, waz obene geschiht.	and no one saw what happened above.
# [Bar 1, Stollen 2 – forge crew, hard, every syllable a hammer]
37279	Ez was ein tac als ander tage,	It was a day like any other day,
41303	diu esse gluot, der zein was heiz.	the forge glowed, the iron was hot.
44974	Do wart der wint so swaer und stille,	Then the wind grew heavy and still,
48790	der rouch gie nider, gel und weiz.	the smoke sank down, yellow and white.
# [Bar 1, Abgesang – both crews together]
52214	Do kam daz weter durch die stat,	Then the poison-weather came through the town,
56250	daz niemen ruoft und niemen bat.	and no one called out, and no one prayed.
59893	Diu tür gie zuo. Der tac wart naht.	The door fell shut. Day turned to night.
# [Chorus – both crews, anvil and pickaxe together]
67203	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
71250	Slahet, daz man ez hoere!	Strike, so that they hear it!
74721	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
78590	Slahet, biz si komen!	Strike, until they come!
# [Bar 2, Stollen 1 – pit crew, growling, then quieter]
83721	Wir sazen tief in unser naht,	We sat deep in our night,
87367	und obene wart ez stiller stunt.	and above it grew ever stiller.
90431	Kein rat, kein wagen, keine stimme –	No wheel, no cart, no voice –
94867	wan ein hamer sluoc. Der was uns kunt.	only a hammer struck. That one we knew.
# [Bar 2, Stollen 2 – forge crew, clipped]
98723	Wir stuonden in dem gelben rouch	We stood in the yellow smoke
102766	und horten unden niht ein wort.	and heard not a word from below.
106410	Do sprach der alte an der esse:	Then the old man at the forge said:
109947	Slahet. Si vindent uns an dem ort.	Strike. They will find us by it.
# [Bar 2, Abgesang – both crews together, slow]
113720	Ein hamer ist ein kleinez lieht,	A hammer is a small light,
117623	doch hoert man in, swa man niht siht.	yet you hear it where you cannot see.
121330	Slac umbe slac: der wec nach hus.	Blow by blow: the way home.
# [Chorus – both crews, anvil and pickaxe together]
128404	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
132527	Slahet, daz man ez hoere!	Strike, so that they hear it!
135998	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
154139	Slahet, biz si komen!	Strike, until they come!	~
# [Break – only one slow hammer on the anvil, far away, pit crew hums toward it]
160296	(Mmmmmmm… mmmmmmm…)	
160329	(Brrrrum… mmmmm… brrrrum…)	
# [Bar 3, Stollen 1 – pit crew, whispered, then rising]
160415	Wir giengen nach dem slage uf	We climbed up toward the blows
164107	durch weter, daz die brust verbran,	through weather that burned the chest,
168032	und kamen uz bi der esse,	and came out beside the forge,
171902	und ieglicher greif eine hant.	and each one grasped a hand.
# [Bar 3, Stollen 2 – forge crew, low, half-time]
175395	Sit sluoc kein hamer mer umbe golt	Since then no hammer struck for gold
178963	und keiner umbe herren, die niht sehent.	and none for lords who do not see.
182979	Er sluoc umbe die, die unden sint –	It struck for those who are below –
186762	daz si wizzen, wa die lebenden stent.	so they know where the living stand.
# [Chorus – both crews, anvil and pickaxe together]
